{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the two angels came.</b> Rashi explains: regarding Lot, it calls them angels. And if you ask: but it is written, 'and the men said to Lot.' Rather, this is what it says: those whom the people of the city called men said — and so you should interpret: to those you called men, do nothing — and likewise, 'and the men seized.'" "<b>And Lot sat in the gate of Sodom.</b> When the merchant finished, he returned to his place and his dwelling by the gate. Therefore, 'and he urged them strongly,' for the place was modest and there was no need to worry there about transgressors, because the eye of transgressors does not rule over it."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:49.433040925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}